Subject: [PATCH] usb: onboard: keep the H432B onboard hub active at runtime

On H432B, suspending the empty NEC hub can stall OHCI register accesses
and normal restart. Connecting a downstream device releases the stall.
Keeping the hub runtime-active permits restart with all sockets empty.

Limit the workaround to the H432B board and its DT-described NEC hub.
Use the USB core runtime-PM API; retain system-sleep callbacks and do
not change either host controller's power-management policy.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [H432B board-specific hardware workaround]

--- a/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c
@@ -635,8 +635,16 @@ static int onboard_dev_usbdev_probe(struct usb_device *udev)
 	err = onboard_dev_add_usbdev(onboard_dev, udev);
 	if (err)
 		return err;

+	/*
+	 * An idle upstream link on this board can stall host register
+	 * accesses during shutdown. System sleep remains supported.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("hims,braillesense-u2") &&
+	    of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "usb409,5a"))
+		usb_disable_autosuspend(udev);
+
 	return 0;
 }

 static void onboard_dev_usbdev_disconnect(struct usb_device *udev)
